            "text": "An efficient implementation in Python that balances memory usage and execution speed by processing the CSV in chunks using Pandas and NumPy vectorized operations.\n\n```python\nimport json\nimport pandas as pd\n\n\ndef main():\n    totals = {}\n    chunksize = 500_000\n\n    for chunk in pd.read_csv(\n        'transactions.csv',\n        usecols=['account_id', 'category', 'amount_cents'],\n        dtype={'account_id': 'int64', 'category': 'str', 'amount_cents': 'int64'},\n        chunksize=chunksize,\n    ):\n        acc = chunk['account_id']\n        mask = (acc % 11) < 7\n        if not mask.any():\n            continue\n\n        sub_acc = acc[mask]\n        sub_cat = chunk.loc[mask, 'category']\n        sub_amt = chunk.loc[mask, 'amount_cents']\n\n        weight = (sub_acc % 97) + 1\n        val = sub_amt * weight\n\n        for cat, s in val.groupby(sub_cat).sum().items():\n            totals[cat] = totals.get(cat, 0) + int(s)\n\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{json.dumps(totals, sort_keys=True)}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n```",
